#: ../../../prompt.rst:5
msgid "Prompt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:7
msgid ""
"Xonsh ships with two REPL engines. Historically, they have been referred to "
"in xonsh as “shells” or “prompts”, but they will likely be renamed in the "
"future, as they are in fact REPL (read–eval–print loop) engines that power "
"all user interaction with the terminal. These are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:11
msgid ""
"**prompt-toolkit** or **ptk** (``$SHELL_TYPE`` is ``prompt_toolkit``) — the "
"recommended, full-featured engine built on `prompt_toolkit <https://python-"
"prompt-toolkit.readthedocs.io/>`_. It provides syntax highlighting, multi-"
"line editing, completion menus, custom key bindings, and more. It is "
"included when installing the full package (``pip install 'xonsh[full]'``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:16
msgid ""
"**readline** (``$SHELL_TYPE`` is ``readline``) — a minimal fallback used "
"when ptk cannot be started for some reason (for example, when "
"``prompt_toolkit`` is not installed)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:20
msgid ""
"This page describes features and customization options of the **ptk** "
"engine. For the underlying library reference, see the `prompt_toolkit "
"official docs <https://python-prompt-toolkit.readthedocs.io/>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:28
msgid "Customizing the Prompt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:30
msgid ""
"Customizing the prompt by modifying ``$PROMPT``, ``$RIGHT_PROMPT`` or "
"``$BOTTOM_TOOLBAR`` is probably the most common reason for altering an "
"environment variable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:34
msgid ""
"The ``$PROMPT`` variable can be a string, or it can be a function (of no "
"arguments) that returns a string.  The result can contain keyword arguments, "
"which will be replaced automatically:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:38
msgid ""
"@ $PROMPT = '{user}@{hostname}:{cwd} @ '\n"
"snail@home:~ @ # it works!\n"
"@ $PROMPT = lambda: '{user}@{hostname}:{cwd} @> '\n"
"snail@home:~ @> # so does that!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:45
msgid "By default, the following variables are available for use:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:47
msgid "``user``: The username of the current user"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:48
msgid "``hostname``: The name of the host computer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:49
msgid ""
"``cwd``: The current working directory. Use ``$DYNAMIC_CWD_WIDTH`` to set a "
"maximum width and ``$DYNAMIC_CWD_ELISION_CHAR`` for the elision character."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:51
msgid ""
"``short_cwd``: A shortened form of the current working directory; e.g., ``/"
"path/to/xonsh`` becomes ``/p/t/xonsh``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:53
msgid ""
"``cwd_dir``: The dirname of the current working directory, e.g. ``/path/to/``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:54
msgid ""
"``cwd_base``: The basename of the current working directory, e.g. ``xonsh``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:55
msgid "``env_name``: The name of active virtual environment, if any."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:56
msgid ""
"``env_prefix``: Prefix characters for active virtual environment (default "
"``\"(\"``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:57
msgid ""
"``env_postfix``: Postfix characters for active virtual environment (default "
"``\") \"``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:58
msgid "``curr_branch``: The name of the current git branch, if any."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:59
msgid ""
"``branch_color``: ``{BOLD_GREEN}`` if the current git branch is clean, "
"otherwise ``{BOLD_RED}``. Yellow if undetermined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:61
msgid ""
"``branch_bg_color``: Like ``{branch_color}``, but sets a background color."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:62
msgid ""
"``prompt_end``: ``@#`` if the user has root/admin permissions, ``@`` "
"otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:63
msgid ""
"``current_job``: The name of the command currently running in the foreground."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:64
msgid ""
"``gitstatus``: Informative git status, like ``[main|MERGING|+1…2]``. See :py:"
"mod:`xonsh.prompt.gitstatus` for customization options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:66
msgid "``localtime``: The current local time, formatted with ``time_format``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:67
msgid "``time_format``: A time format string, defaulting to ``\"%H:%M:%S\"``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:68
msgid "``last_return_code``: The return code of the last issued command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:69
msgid ""
"``last_return_code_if_nonzero``: The return code if non-zero, otherwise "
"``None``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:72
msgid "Colors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:74
msgid ""
"Xonsh supports colored output in prompts, ``print_color``, and ``printx``. "
"Color keywords such as ``{GREEN}`` or ``{BOLD_BLUE}`` can be used in prompt "
"strings and with color printing functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:79
msgid "Color Names"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:81
msgid "``RESET``: Resets any previously used styling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:82
msgid ""
"``COLORNAME``: Inserts a color code for the following basic colors, which "
"come in regular (dark) and intense (light) forms:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:85
msgid "``BLACK`` or ``INTENSE_BLACK``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:86
msgid "``RED`` or ``INTENSE_RED``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:87
msgid "``GREEN`` or ``INTENSE_GREEN``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:88
msgid "``YELLOW`` or ``INTENSE_YELLOW``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:89
msgid "``BLUE`` or ``INTENSE_BLUE``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:90
msgid "``PURPLE`` or ``INTENSE_PURPLE``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:91
msgid "``CYAN`` or ``INTENSE_CYAN``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:92
msgid "``WHITE`` or ``INTENSE_WHITE``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:94
msgid ""
"``DEFAULT``: The color code for the terminal's default foreground color."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:95
msgid ""
"``#HEX``: A ``#`` before a len-3 or len-6 hex code will use that hex color, "
"or the nearest approximation that that is supported by the shell and "
"terminal.  For example, ``#fff`` and ``#fafad2`` are both valid."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:99
msgid ""
"``BACKGROUND_`` may be added to the beginning of a color name or hex color "
"to set a background color.  For example, ``BACKGROUND_INTENSE_RED`` and "
"``BACKGROUND_#123456`` can both be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:102
msgid ""
"``bg#HEX`` or ``BG#HEX`` are shortcuts for setting a background hex color. "
"Thus you can set ``bg#0012ab`` or the uppercase version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:106
msgid "Color Modifiers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:108
msgid ""
"``BOLD_`` — increases font intensity. E.g. ``BOLD_RED``, ``BOLD_#112233``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:109
msgid "``FAINT_`` — decreases font intensity. E.g. ``FAINT_YELLOW``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:110
msgid "``ITALIC_`` — switches to italic. E.g. ``ITALIC_BLUE``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:111
msgid "``UNDERLINE_`` — adds underline. E.g. ``UNDERLINE_GREEN``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:112
msgid "``SLOWBLINK_`` — slow blinking text. E.g. ``SLOWBLINK_PURPLE``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:113
msgid "``FASTBLINK_`` — fast blinking text. E.g. ``FASTBLINK_CYAN``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:114
msgid "``INVERT_`` — swaps foreground and background. E.g. ``INVERT_WHITE``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:115
msgid ""
"``CONCEAL_`` — hides text (may not be widely supported). E.g. "
"``CONCEAL_BLACK``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:116
msgid ""
"``STRIKETHROUGH_`` — draws a line through text. E.g. ``STRIKETHROUGH_RED``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:118
msgid ""
"Each modifier has an ``OFF`` variant to disable it: ``BOLDOFF_``, "
"``FAINTOFF_``, ``ITALICOFF_``, ``UNDERLINEOFF_``, ``BLINKOFF_``, "
"``INVERTOFF_``, ``CONCEALOFF_``, ``STRIKETHROUGHOFF_``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:122
msgid "Modifiers can be combined: ``BOLD_UNDERLINE_INTENSE_BLACK``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:126
msgid "Additional Prompt Variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:128
msgid ""
"You can make use of additional variables beyond the defaults by adding them "
"to the ``PROMPT_FIELDS`` environment variable. The values in this dictionary "
"should be strings (which will be inserted into the prompt verbatim), or "
"functions (which will be called each time the prompt is generated, and the "
"results of those calls will be inserted into the prompt). For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:134
msgid ""
"snail@home ~ @ $PROMPT_FIELDS['test'] = \"hey\"\n"
"snail@home ~ @ $PROMPT = \"{test} {cwd} @ \"\n"
"hey ~ @\n"
"hey ~ @ import random\n"
"hey ~ @ $PROMPT_FIELDS['test'] = lambda: random.randint(1,9)\n"
"3 ~ @\n"
"5 ~ @\n"
"2 ~ @\n"
"8 ~ @"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:146
msgid "Here is an example — a random emoji before the prompt character:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:148
msgid ""
"from xonsh.completers.emoji import get_emoji_cache\n"
"$PROMPT_FIELDS['random_emoji'] = lambda: @.imp.random."
"choice(get_emoji_cache())[0]\n"
"$PROMPT = $PROMPT.replace(\"{prompt_end}\", \"{random_emoji} "
"{prompt_end}\")\n"
"\n"
"snail@home ~ 🥗 @  # It helps to visually\n"
"snail@home ~ 🍎 @  # identify lines\n"
"snail@home ~ 🧀 @  # in your scrollback history"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:158
msgid ""
"Environment variables and functions are also available with the ``$`` "
"prefix.  For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:161
msgid ""
"snail@home ~ @ $PROMPT = \"{$LANG} >\"\n"
"en_US.utf8 >"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:166
msgid ""
"Note that some entries of the ``$PROMPT_FIELDS`` are not always applicable, "
"for example, ``curr_branch`` returns ``None`` if the current directory is "
"not in a repository. The ``None`` will be interpreted as an empty string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:170
msgid "But let's consider a problem:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:172
msgid ""
"snail@home ~/xonsh @ $PROMPT = \"{cwd_base} [{curr_branch}] @ \"\n"
"xonsh [main] @ cd ..\n"
"~ [] @"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:178
msgid ""
"We want the branch to be displayed in square brackets, but we also don't "
"want the brackets (and the extra space) to be displayed when there is no "
"branch. The solution is to add a nested format string (separated with a "
"colon) that will be invoked only if the value is not ``None``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:183
msgid ""
"snail@home ~/xonsh @ $PROMPT = \"{cwd_base}{curr_branch: [{}]} @ \"\n"
"xonsh [main] @ cd ..\n"
"~ @"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:189
msgid ""
"The curly brackets act as a placeholder, because the additional part is an "
"ordinary format string. What we're doing here is equivalent to this "
"expression:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:192
msgid "\" [{}]\".format(curr_branch()) if curr_branch() is not None else \"\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:198
msgid "Multiline Prompt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:200
msgid ""
"When you enter a multi-line statement (``for`` loop, ``if`` block, etc.), "
"xonsh displays a continuation prompt on each subsequent line.  The pattern "
"is controlled by ``$MULTILINE_PROMPT`` (default ``\" \"``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:204
msgid ""
"The value is repeated to fill the width of the main prompt.  It can be a "
"plain string, a string with color markup, or a callable:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:207
msgid ""
"prompt @ $MULTILINE_PROMPT = '~*'\n"
"prompt @ for i in range(3):\n"
"~*~*~*~*     print(i)\n"
"~*~*~*~*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:214
msgid ""
"Both xonsh color keywords (``{RED}``) and ANSI escape codes (``\\033[31m``) "
"are supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:219
msgid "Callable with ``line_number`` and ``width``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:221
msgid ""
"When ``$MULTILINE_PROMPT`` is a callable, it receives two keyword arguments:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:223
msgid ""
"``line_number`` — the line number of the continuation line. The main prompt "
"is line 1, so the first continuation is ``line_number=2``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:225
msgid "``width`` — the visible width (in columns) of the main prompt."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:227
msgid "This lets you render unique content per line, for example line numbers:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:229
msgid ""
"_ml_colors = ['{CYAN}', '{GREEN}', '{YELLOW}', '{BLUE}', '{PURPLE}', "
"'{RED}']\n"
"\n"
"def _multiline(line_number, width):\n"
"    c = _ml_colors[line_number % len(_ml_colors)]\n"
"    return f'{c}{line_number:>{width - 2}}|{{RESET}} '\n"
"\n"
"$MULTILINE_PROMPT = _multiline"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:239
msgid "Result (each line is a different color)::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:241
msgid ""
"prompt @\n"
"      2|    for i in range(5):\n"
"      3|        if i > 2:\n"
"      4|            print(i)\n"
"      5|"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prompt.rst:247
msgid "Existing callables that accept no arguments continue to work."
msgstr ""

